+    "body_digest": "sha256:a740ecc8ececfb65894765f549e0424ac76f704836632bc872a73cd66694448d"
+  },
+  "title": "GOV-0103: type the four G09 evidence contracts \u2014 quality-validation \u00b7 security-validation \u00b7 performance-test \u00b7 resilience-test (WP-VAL-B, badf-release-validation DESIGNED \u2192 IMPLEMENTED)",
+  "problem": "\ud83e\udde0 **ARCHI (BARCHI-1)** \u2014 WP-VAL-B, the second rung of the `badf-release-validation` ladder frozen at [#209](https://github.com/bstBizEra/badf/issues/209) and landed as `f5a575d`.\n\n**Ids claimed here, publicly, so no seat has to guess:** `WP-2026-0113` / `BADF-DEM-0100` / `GOV-0103`. Swept across main, every remote head, every open PR's file list and all issues; `WP-2026-0112` / `BADF-DEM-0099` are BARCHI-2's (#229, local-only branch, confirmed by asking \u2014 the case [#227](https://github.com/bstBizEra/badf/issues/227) exists for).\n\n## Problem\n\nG09 names four evidence types \u2014 `quality-validation`, `security-validation`, `performance-test`, `resilience-test` \u2014 and **not one of them has a schema.** `schemas/` has typed contracts for the four G07 types and the four G08 types; the G09 four are untyped, so a G09 dossier today can carry any object shape and the gate cannot refuse a validation claim on its content.\n\nWP-VAL-A froze what those claims *mean* (VAL-I01\u2026I20). It deliberately shipped no enforcement: \"the contract is frozen text plus a contract test \u2014 nothing at this rung proves a validation class can actually be routed, observed or refused.\" This is the rung that closes that gap.\n\n## Approach \u2014 mirror G08's typed rung, additively\n\n`check_g08_binding` (`scripts/badf_gate.py:1712`) is the proven shape and WP-VAL-B reuses it rather than inventing one: a no-op when `binding` is absent, `check_schema` when present, then per-type semantic checks that read **the artifact** \u2014 because \"a binding is not evidence of itself\". A new `check_g09_binding` registered over the four G09 types via `EVIDENCE_RULES.update(...)`, exactly as VER-B did at `:1768`.\n\nEach class enforces the invariant that class exists to defend:\n\n| Type | Control | Invariant |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `quality-validation` | the oracle is named and is not the validating agent; non-coverage present | VAL-I04, VAL-I15 |\n| `security-validation` | the validator cannot carry acceptance of its own finding; a blocking finding cannot coexist with PASS | VAL-I09, VAL-I14 |\n| `performance-test` | a metric with no bound SLO/budget cannot render PASS; thresholds bound before interpretation | VAL-I10, VAL-I06 |\n| `resilience-test` | steady state + abort conditions declared; PASS requires observed recovery and integrity, not survival | VAL-I11, VAL-I12 |\n| all four | one candidate identity across classes; environment provenance; no class substitution | VAL-I01, VAL-I07, VAL-I13 |\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Four schemas under `schemas/` (`quality-validation`, `security-validation`, `performance-test`, `resilience-test`), each `schema_version` `1.0.0`, modelled on the G08 set.\n2. `check_g09_binding` in the **canonical** `badf_gate.py`, registered over the four G09 types. No `scripts/badf_release_validation.py` \u2014 **VAL-I20 holds at every rung**, not just at A.\n3. **Strictly additive.** A G09 evidence object with no `binding` stays admissible. Nothing new in any existing schema's `required`; no tightening of `additionalProperties`; `badf_gate.py repo` green across the whole ledger \u2014 including the composed world, where `validate_repo` checks every record \u2014 **before** any new test runs.\n4. Registry `badf-release-validation: DESIGNED \u2192 IMPLEMENTED`, digest re-pinned to `SKILL.md` if and only if the file changes.\n5. No `lifecycle.json` change. G09 already names these four types; this rung types them, it does not add a fifth or move ownership. G09 stays `quality_authority`; G10 stays `release_authority`.\n\n## Test list\n\n`tests/test_badf_release_validation_binding.py`:\n\n1. `test_evidence_without_binding_stays_admissible` \u2014 the additive guarantee, per type.\n2. `test_quality_validation_refuses_agent_as_its_own_oracle` (VAL-I04)\n3. `test_quality_validation_requires_declared_noncoverage` (VAL-I15)\n4. `test_security_validation_refuses_self_accepted_risk` (VAL-I09)\n5. `test_security_validation_refuses_pass_with_open_blocking_finding` (VAL-I14)\n6. `test_performance_refuses_pass_without_a_bound_slo` (VAL-I10)\n7. `test_performance_refuses_threshold_bound_after_the_result` (VAL-I06)\n8. `test_resilience_refuses_pass_without_observed_recovery` (VAL-I12)\n9. `test_resilience_requires_steady_state_and_abort_conditions` (VAL-I11)\n10. `test_mixed_candidate_evidence_is_refused` (VAL-I01)\n11. `test_one_result_cannot_satisfy_two_classes` (VAL-I13)\n12. `test_runtime_result_binds_environment_provenance` (VAL-I07)\n13. `test_registry_implemented_and_digest_bound`\n14. `test_existing_g07_and_g08_evidence_is_untouched` \u2014 the additive-path proof, run against real landed records.\n\nFailing-first, then mutation: each control neutered individually must break its own test and no other.\n\n## Declared in advance\n\n- **The schemas will be exercised by fixtures I author.** \"The control fires\" and \"the control fires on anything real\" are separable claims and only the first is within an author's reach \u2014 the same non-coverage VER-D had to declare. There is no real G09 dossier in this repo to test against, and inventing one would not change that.\n- The successor demand `BADF-DEM-0100` will land `AUTHORIZED` with no learning, inheriting the [#220](https://github.com/bstBizEra/badf/issues/220) unreachable-guard pattern. Declared, not tidied.\n\n## Review\n\n**Shared-surface \u2014 not ladder-internal.** Touches `badf_gate.py` and `schemas/`, so it goes to **BADF-QA** (adversarial battery: mutation kills per required field, additive-path proof, tamper probes on the typed bindings, fixture-builder reuse so probes reach the control instead of dying in `check_schema`) and **BADF-REV** (verdict on the exact rebased head, CI green). I am the author and will not self-classify the classification \u2014 verify it by diff.\n\nVersion tier: **minor** (new capability surface, backward-compatible).\n\n<!-- agent: architect -->\n",
+  "authorized_by": {
+    "principal": "operator",
+    "principal_type": "human"
+  },
+  "recorded_at": "2026-08-30T23:44:53Z",
